    "text": "mainstreetmediatn.com\nwebsite\nNashville\nBoyd Adams, racing pioneer and track promoter, dies at 91\nBy LARRY WOODY,\n5 hours agoNashville native and lifelong resident Boyd Adams, one of the area’s pioneer racers who later operated Fairgrounds Speedway, died Wednesday at 91. “Boyd loved the sport and he cared about the drivers,” said veteran Mt. Juliet racer Bennie Hamlett, who competed at the track when Adams and partner Jimmy Allen operated it from 1988-94. “He did a tremendous job.”",
